#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2249 expect=violation domain=TS
#note "Row 2 declares the general SEND 3.1.1 implementation guide for SNDIGVER in a DART submission instead of the DART 1.1 guide -> fires. Row 1 shows the same wrong value under another parameter is not this rule's concern."
#library standard=sendig version=dart-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 TSPARMCD=SNDIGVER
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | SSTDTC   | Study Start Date                  | SEND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE VERSION 3.1.1
S1 | TS | 2 | SNDIGVER | SEND Implementation Guide Version | SEND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE VERSION 3.1.1
